  "findings": [
    "Four failed exchanges have correlated TCP/IP Not locally destined drops: two requests and two replies, across Windows 2022 and 2025. All have unchanged traffic class zero.",
    "Each of these four drop events has one same-host TCP/IP Event 1215 outer-address/time candidate in the preceding ten microseconds. Native transportProtocol is zero, reason is 2. Snapshot mapping places Windows 2022 IfIndex 18 and Windows 2025 IfIndex 17 in compartment 2 on link-local adapters, distinct from the destination EC2 address adapters.",
    "The Windows 2022 to w1 failed request has 16 sender appearances and no decoded request or reply in the site capture. The adjacent successful samples appear in the site capture. This brackets an observation gap; it does not locate a specific gateway, tunnel, or network loss.",
    "The Windows 2025 original exporter completed after the SSM wrapper timed out. Source hashes verified all fourteen original Windows artifacts and both extracted text files before cleanup. No capture or sampler was replayed.",
    "Post-capture Get-NetCompartment identifies compartment 2 as DR on both versions. HNS reports Calico and External overlay networks sharing a lower layer and DR MAC on each host. This is native mapping context, not evidence that the External network is obsolete or the cause of loss."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Event 1215 has no packet ID; nearby events provide interface context and do not independently identify a packet or establish the cause.",
    "Interface mappings are pre-capture snapshots; no claim is made that they prove every instantaneous state.",
    "Windows 2025 original stop output was not recovered, so this report does not assert zero lost ETW events for that host. Linux tcpdump reported zero kernel drops.",
    "PCAP appearances do not prove application delivery; absence is not proof of non-delivery. Cross-host wall clocks are not transit-latency measurements.",
    "This diagnostic run cannot qualify Windows lifecycle support, a mitigation, image promotion, or a release."
  ],
